<title>SPAIN: Spain employers say rate cut paves way for growth.</title>
<headline>Spain employers say rate cut paves way for growth.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 25-basis-point interest rate cut by the Bank of Spain on Friday paves the way for greater domestic growth this year, employers association CEOE said.</p>
<p>The central bank's key money rate is now 5.75 percent.</p>
<p>The rate cut also lifts doubts regarding the peseta's entry into monetary union from the start of the project, CEOE said.</p>
<p>The group was expecting further monetary easing this year, given economic fundamentals.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
